From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:03:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/48] net: airoha: ploam: reject a Ranging_Adjustment that
 wraps the EqD

handle_ranging_adjustment() computed the new equalisation delay as
pp->eqd -/+ offset in u32 without any bound. A decrease larger than the
ranged EqD (or an increase past U32_MAX) wrapped around, and the
resulting value went straight to adjust_eqd_o5(), which would move every
upstream burst by an absurd amount and take the ONU off the PON.

An EqD is a non-negative bit count, so such a message cannot be a valid
adjustment. Keep the ranged EqD, log the message (rate limited) and do
not acknowledge it, so the OLT sees the command was not executed.

The Huawei OLT this was tested against never sends Ranging_Adjustment;
the change only affects malformed messages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.c
index 6137733..898fd30 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.c
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@
  * content bytes are compared, matching the seven-byte vendor comparison.
  */
 
+#include <linux/limits.h>
+#include <linux/printk.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/random.h>
 #include <linux/string.h>
@@ -582,6 +584,19 @@ static void handle_ranging_adjustment(struct ploam_priv *pp,
 		/* c[0] BE: bits[7:2]=resv, bit[1]=s_bit, bit[0]=resv */
 		s_bit = (c[0] >> 1) & 1;
 		eqd_offset = get_unaligned_be32(&c[1]);
+		/*
+		 * The EqD is an unsigned bit count. A decrease larger than the
+		 * current EqD, or an increase that wraps it, cannot be a valid
+		 * adjustment: applying it would move the bursts by ~2^32 bits.
+		 * Keep the ranged EqD and do not acknowledge the message.
+		 */
+		if (s_bit ? eqd_offset > pp->eqd :
+			    eqd_offset > U32_MAX - pp->eqd) {
+			pr_warn_ratelimited("airoha-ploam: ignoring Ranging_Adjustment %c%u on EqD %u: out of range\n",
+					    s_bit ? '-' : '+', eqd_offset,
+					    pp->eqd);
+			return;
+		}
 		if (eqd_offset != 0) {
 			u32 new_eqd = s_bit ? pp->eqd - eqd_offset
 					    : pp->eqd + eqd_offset;
